{
  "image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/615iz6LG9qL._AC_SX342_SY445_QL70_FMwebp_.jpg",
  "url": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0F7M6BN1F",
  "name": "STP GOODS Russian Folk Costume 'Kokoshnik' Headdress",
  "offers": {
    "price": 39.99,
    "priceCurrency": "$"
  },
  "brand": {
    "slogan": "STP GOODS"
  },
  "description": "Step into the elegance of Russian tradition with the \"Elena Kokoshnik Headdress (Red).\" This exquisite headdress, inspired by traditional Russian kokoshnik designs, is a perfect blend of cultural heritage and sophisticated craftsmanship, making it an ideal accessory for special occasions and cultural events. Description: The \"Elena Kokoshnik Headdress (Red)\" is a beautifully crafted piece that reflects the rich cultural history of Russia. Traditionally worn by women and girls during festive occasions, the kokoshnik is known for its distinctive shape and ornate decoration. This red version of the kokoshnik features intricate detailing, luxurious materials, and a regal design that makes it a standout accessory. Adorned with delicate beadwork, embroidery, and embellishments, the headdress showcases a stunning combination of traditional artistry and modern elegance. The vibrant red color symbolizes prosperity and joy, making it perfect for celebrations, performances, and cultural events. The headdress is designed to sit comfortably on the head, with a secure fit that ensures it stays in place throughout the event. Whether you're dressing up for a traditional Russian celebration, a theatrical performance, or simply want to add a touch of cultural elegance to your outfit, the \"Elena Kokoshnik Headdress (Red)\" is the perfect choice. It is a timeless accessory that pays homage to Russian heritage while adding a touch of sophistication to any ensemble.The word \"kokoshnik\" is derived from the archaic Slavic word \"kokosh,\" meaning hen. It is an old, traditional headdress in the shape of a wave crest, that is an integral part of a holiday women's Russian folk costume. In the olden days Russian ladies bought kokoshniks from special masters whose addresses were passed on as big secrets. The story of each woman was hidden on her kokoshnik in the shape and the decoration style on the headdress – ribbons, flowers, beads, lace, pearls, gold embroidery, and gems – these stylistically presented such information as where she lives in Russia, her material and social status, as well as her family status. The shape of a kokoshnik depended on the hair style and fashion on in a particular area. A kokoshnik is an unusual and very feminine accessory for Russian fashion lovers of the past.",
