      {
        "username": "Big Dong",
        "userId": "amzn1.account.AE6B3YYXT3HWEFK6U2HW2WLX7PMA",
        "userProfileLink": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AE6B3YYXT3HWEFK6U2HW2WLX7PMA",
        "ratingScore": 4,
        "reviewTitle": "Stylish and Cozy Shawl, Just a Bit Fragile",
        "reviewDescription": "The media could not be loaded.\n                \n            \n                \n            \n            \n        \n    \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    This is a lovely shawl with gorgeous paisley patterns and lots of fine tassels — about 10 threads in each group — all around the edges. It’s lightweight and a bit see-through, but still warm enough because it's made of velour. It's super versatile too — perfect as a scarf or shawl from fall through spring.The front side has a soft, cozy, velvet-like feel where the patterns are, with a slightly embossed texture, while the back side is a flat base but still nice and soft.I would have been really happy to add it to my wardrobe if it had been better sewn. Unfortunately, I accidentally pulled out a thread when it got caught on a rough spot on my finger. When I looked closely at the tassels, I noticed that some groups are securely fixed, but others can come loose if you pull on them — you can see it happen in my video.That means you’ll need to be careful not to snag or lose threads, even when washing it.It’s a bit disappointing, but still, it’s the kind of piece that's great to have — it can instantly turn a simple outfit into something stylish without much effort.",
        "date": "2025-04-27",
        "position": 6,
        "reviewedIn": "Reviewed in the United States on April 27, 2025",
        "reviewId": "R22C7TKHZ0FS5H",
        "reviewUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/customer-reviews/R22C7TKHZ0FS5H/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_ttl?ie=UTF8",
        "reviewImages": [],
