  "name": "Hohloma Russian Bear Ukrainian Traditional Pattern T-Shirt",
  "offers": {
    "price": null,
    "priceCurrency": null
  },
  "brand": {
    "slogan": "Heritage Design House"
  },
  "description": "Hohloma is a style of painting mostly used to decorate wooden goods and furniture from 17th century Russia onwards. Here I put this pattern on the California Bear. It signifies the influence of Russian, Ukrainian, Eastern European and slavic immigrants on the USA. This is the slav answer to paisley patterns.",
