      },
      {
        "username": "Silence Dogood II",
        "userId": "amzn1.account.AGXWBIGIAWUMZ6P7T2W5M2TXMLFQ",
        "userProfileLink": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AGXWBIGIAWUMZ6P7T2W5M2TXMLFQ",
        "ratingScore": 4,
        "reviewTitle": "Beautiful, well made and decently priced but just a little too small for most people",
        "reviewDescription": "This is a vibrantly beautiful print scarf. I'm not as fond of the fringe but my sister likes it. It is deceiving though, when you read the dimensions initially I thought it was the exterior sizes but the dimensions are given diagonally so it's not as large as you think. I've included a picture of my sister wearing it as a shawl. She is 5'6 and wears a woman's 12/large. As you can see it doesn't quite make it as a shawl for her. So unless the person you intend it for is very tiny and petite, it's not going to quite cut it. I have decided to use this on an antique table as a tablecloth. I have this cool square side table and this looks fantastic on it. So tiny people, this is the shell for you. Normal size people, this will be a cover for a side table. Like I said it is beautiful, decently priced and well made - but it's just too small.",
        "date": "2025-09-18",
        "position": 2,
        "reviewedIn": "Reviewed in the United States on September 18, 2025",
        "reviewId": "RVLYE7ESDGX9",
