      {
        "username": "Esbe Hennessy",
        "userId": "amzn1.account.AEU7RWLBZSCQD7TJTANPOWXXZ5VA",
        "userProfileLink": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AEU7RWLBZSCQD7TJTANPOWXXZ5VA",
        "ratingScore": 4,
        "reviewTitle": "Very nice shawl to take the chill away",
        "reviewDescription": "This is a very nice shawl. It's soft, a great color that is versatile, and provides enough warmth to take the chill away. However, I very much doubt that it has much, if any, true pashmina. I think this partly due to the price, it's a great price for this shawl, but far too low for true pashmina. Also because pashmina is not blended with polyester. But that detail aside, I still think it's a great shawl.I got this for my mother who spends a lot of time sitting at her computer playing games. I know sometimes she'd like something to throw over her shoulders when it's just a little chilly, but not cold enough to need warmer clothes. The fact that it has a subtle loop built in to keep it closed is great, that way it's not going to drive her crazy by constantly opening or one side falling off. It also looks fine if you don't use the loop and just want it hanging open.It's made quite well, all the stitches are in place and no threads sticking out. It's a nice thickness, enough to provide a little warmth and comfort without being too heavy. It's just the right size to fit over the shoulders and upper back without feeling like you're just wearing a blanket. I can't wait to give this to my mother at Christmas. I know she's going to love it.",
        "date": "2025-11-04",
        "position": 3,
        "reviewedIn": "Reviewed in the United States on November 4, 2025",
        "reviewId": "RDUBZYQI12K0F",
        "reviewUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/customer-reviews/RDUBZYQI12K0F/ref=cm_cr_dp_d_rvw_ttl?ie=UTF8",
