      {
        "username": "SplkdancerReviews",
        "userId": "amzn1.account.AER5RVWNZ7QJBERLMNNJ2GGLBSSA",
        "userProfileLink": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AER5RVWNZ7QJBERLMNNJ2GGLBSSA",
        "ratingScore": 4,
        "reviewTitle": "Soft but cheap acrylic wrap, decent edging and looks better at a distance",
        "reviewDescription": "The brown wrap is a very cheap acrylic item. It is a decent-sized triangle with a loop that is stitched on. The loop is knitted in, which is impressive. When you wrap it around, you can tuck the end through the loop, creating a triangle down your back.It's a decent size but a bit slippery, so it slips out of the little auto loop easily. The edges are knitted but feel the same as the fabric. The top edge has a bit of a border. It's not super high quality and looks cheap up close, but for something to wrap around to keep you warm. It is not itchy and feels soft but feels cheap - definitely not wool. Best part is: it's a decent color.",
        "date": "2025-11-11",
        "position": 7,
        "reviewedIn": "Reviewed in the United States on November 11, 2025",
