      {
        "username": "WAMK",
        "userId": null,
        "userProfileLink": null,
        "ratingScore": 5,
        "reviewTitle": "Elegant and incredibly soft for any occasion",
        "reviewDescription": "I bought this black pashmina wrap to wear over an evening dress for a winter wedding, and I could not be happier with how it looked and felt. The fabric is surprisingly soft and has that luxurious, high-end feel that you usually only get with much more expensive cashmere. It provides a perfect amount of warmth without being overly bulky, which allowed me to stay cozy during the ceremony while still looking elegant. The triangle shape is a clever design choice because it drapes naturally over the shoulders and stays in place much better than a traditional rectangular scarf, making it feel more like a tailored poncho.What I love most is how versatile this piece has turned out to be for my everyday wardrobe. Since the wedding, I have been wearing it as a casual wrap over my favorite sweaters and jeans, and it adds an instant touch of sophistication to a basic outfit. The knit is tight and durable, showing no signs of pilling or loose threads even after several wears and being folded in my bag. The deep black color is rich and hasn't faded, making it a timeless staple that works for both formal events and running errands on a chilly day. If you are looking for a gift or a treat for yourself that combines comfort with style, this wrap is a fantastic find.",
        "date": "2025-12-22",
        "position": 3,
        "reviewedIn": "Reviewed in Canada on December 22, 2025",
        "reviewId": "REU23A47HIBQT",
        "reviewUrl": null,
